<title>DUBAI: Second Iraqi tanker set to leave Mina al-Bakr.</title>
<headline>Second Iraqi tanker set to leave Mina al-Bakr.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 272,000 deadweight tonne Leonidas tanker is preparing to leave the Mina al-Bakr export terminal with Iraqi crude, Gulf shipping sources said Thursday.</p>
<p>The tanker, chartered by U.S. independent oil trader Bayoil, is Iraq's second export cargo from the Middle East Gulf under the United Nations &quot;oil-for-food&quot; deal.</p>
<p>&quot;Leonidas gets under way in 45 minutes,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>Tanker Star Africa, chartered by U.S. Coastal Corp, left the terminal on Tuesday becoming Iraq's first export from the Gulf in six years.</p>
<p>The U.N. on Wednesday said it had approved 13 contracts under the oil for food deal which allows Iraq to export $2 billion of oil over six months for humanitarian supplies.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255.</p>
